# CODEOWNERS - policy/CI/hook file protection (agentadhere Phase 5, IPD r2ks4k E-02).
#
# This file, TOGETHER WITH a GitHub "Require review from Code Owners" branch-protection rule that a
# repo admin must ENABLE (see docs/branch-protection.md), makes the policy engine, the CI workflow
# definitions, and the local-hook definitions require an owner review before they can be weakened
# (findings bu9yij 7.8). HONEST LIMIT: a CODEOWNERS file by itself enforces NOTHING - it only takes
# effect when branch protection with "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled on the default
# branch (a remote repo-admin action the local toolkit cannot self-enforce).
#
# ACTION REQUIRED (human): replace @OWNER below with the actual maintainer handle or team
# (e.g. @your-org/maintainers). It is left as a placeholder deliberately so no maintainer identity is
# committed to this public repo (see CONTRIBUTING.md on not embedding maintainer identity).

# The shared policy engine every layer (hooks, CI, aw check) depends on.
/agent_workflows/check_engine.py            @OWNER

# The local git-hook definitions (the phase-4 gates that delegate to the engine).
/agent_workflows/hooks/                      @OWNER

# The CI / workflow definitions - the authoritative repository boundary must not be weakened
# without an owner review.
/.github/workflows/                          @OWNER
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @OWNER

# The branch-protection policy document itself.
/docs/branch-protection.md                   @OWNER
